<title>ARGENTINA: Argentina auctions $750 mln in bonds at 8.58 pct.</title>
<headline>Argentina auctions $750 mln in bonds at 8.58 pct.</headline>
<dateline>BUENOS AIRES 1997-06-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Argentina sold $750 million in five year Bonte Treasury bonds at a cut-off yield of 8.58 percent, the Economy Ministry said Thursday.</p>
<p>The issue price was 1006.60. There were bids totaling $4.32 billion giving a bid-to-cover ratio of 5.76 times. The coupon on the bond is 8.75 percent.  </p>
<p>This is the second tranche of the bond that matures on May 9, 2002, following an issue of the same magnitude last month.</p>
<p>It will be raised to a total of $2.0 billion.</p>
<p>This is Argentina's longest maturity Bonte in the local market.</p>
<p>((--Gary Regenstreif, Buenos Aires newsroom, 541 318-0618))</p>
